  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Awards Women&apos;s Leadership Initiative 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Awards Women&apos;s Leadership Initiative 2.0, renamed as Women Leading and Influencing (WLI), will be a continuation of the current program (INM152). Women Leading and Influencing is a four-year (2022-2026) $8 million on-award and reintegration enrichment initiative, supporting female and male Australia Awards scholars and alumni to develop the skills, networks and capabilities to effectively lead and influence on development issues in their countries. WLI also helps to deepen Australia&#x2019;s relationship with our Pacific neighbours. The new phase will also build a cadre of male Australia Awards scholars and alumni who are supporting and promoting women as influencers and change agents. With an initial focus on the Pacific region, the program has the potential to be scaled out to other geographic regions, such as Southeast Asia. https://www.wliprogram.org/</narrative>
  </description>
